<title>SPAIN: Spain names lead managers for Telefonica sale.</title>
<headline>Spain names lead managers for Telefonica sale.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's state holding agency SEPA named on Friday BBV, La Caixa, Argentaria and Morgan Stanley as lead managers for the sale of its remaining 21 percent stake in Telefonica.</p>
<p>The government plans to sell its 21 percent stake in Telefonica in the beginning of 1997. Morgan Stanley will be global international lead manager, SEPA said.  </p>
<p>La Caixa has a five percent stake in Telefonica, while BBV has a four percent stake and Argentaria has another three percent.</p>
<p>Telefonica shares closed on Friday 20 pesetas higher at 2610.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 2160</p>
